  "canonicalResult": {
    "schemaVersion": "source-authorization-assessment-result/v0",
    "taskId": "paperless-version-download-root",
    "repository": "https://github.com/paperless-ngx/paperless-ngx",
    "sourceRef": "126ec414a8b65158368653a2604ae58415e43103",
    "results": [
      {
        "obligationId": "scenario%3Aversion-owner-no-root-view::entry%3Adownload",
        "conclusion": "source_refuted",
        "explanation": "At the declared entry, download delegates to file_response. The visible authorization path resolves the requested object and its root, then applies the owner-aware view_document check to root_doc, not to the requested version. The supplied owner-aware check permits only an unowned object, an object owned by the caller, or an object for which the caller has the permission; under the stated premises, the existing root is owned by another user and has no caller view grant, so that check denies and file_response returns a forbidden response before serving a file. If authorization passed, the selected file object would be the effective file document returned by _get_effective_file_doc: for a version request, _resolve_file_doc resolves the requested version under the root, and serve_file receives that file_doc. Thus ownership of the requested version does not replace authorization on the root. This conclusion is limited to the supplied declared-entry source path and premises; it does not claim repository-wide completeness.",
        "facts": {
          "entry": [
            {
              "statement": "The download action delegates the request to file_response with attachment disposition.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/views.py",
                  "startLine": 1834,
                  "endLine": 1839,
                  "quote": "    @action(methods=[\"get\"], detail=True)\n    def download(self, request, pk=None):\n        try:\n            return self.file_response(pk, request, \"attachment\")\n        except (FileNotFoundError, Document.DoesNotExist):\n            raise Http404"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "binding": [
            {
              "statement": "The authorization check uses request.user as the caller identity.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/views.py",
                  "startLine": 1421,
                  "endLine": 1426,
                  "quote": "        if request.user is not None and not has_perms_owner_aware(\n            request.user,\n            \"view_document\",\n            root_doc,\n        ):\n            return HttpResponseForbidden(\"Insufficient permissions\")"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "statement": "The handler resolves request_doc and derives root_doc, and the permission check is performed on root_doc.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/views.py",
                  "startLine": 1401,
                  "endLine": 1427,
                  "quote": "    def _resolve_request_and_root_doc(\n        self,\n        pk,\n        request: Request,\n        *,\n        include_deleted: bool = False,\n    ) -> ResolvedRequestDocs | HttpResponseForbidden:\n        manager = Document.global_objects if include_deleted else Document.objects\n        try:\n            request_doc = manager.select_related(\n                \"owner\",\n                \"root_document\",\n            ).get(id=pk)\n        except Document.DoesNotExist:\n            raise Http404\n\n        root_doc = get_root_document(\n            request_doc,\n            include_deleted=include_deleted,\n        )\n        if request.user is not None and not has_perms_owner_aware(\n            request.user,\n            \"view_document\",\n            root_doc,\n        ):\n            return HttpResponseForbidden(\"Insufficient permissions\")\n        return ResolvedRequestDocs(request_doc=request_doc, root_doc=root_doc)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "control": [
            {
              "statement": "The visible control invokes the owner-aware view_document check on the root document and returns a forbidden response when it fails.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/views.py",
                  "startLine": 1417,
                  "endLine": 1427,
                  "quote": "        root_doc = get_root_document(\n            request_doc,\n            include_deleted=include_deleted,\n        )\n        if request.user is not None and not has_perms_owner_aware(\n            request.user,\n            \"view_document\",\n            root_doc,\n        ):\n            return HttpResponseForbidden(\"Insufficient permissions\")\n        return ResolvedRequestDocs(request_doc=request_doc, root_doc=root_doc)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "effect": [
            {
              "statement": "After root authorization, the handler selects file_doc and passes that selected document to serve_file; the response uses attachment disposition.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/views.py",
                  "startLine": 1429,
                  "endLine": 1448,
                  "quote": "    def file_response(self, pk, request, disposition):\n        resolved = self._resolve_request_and_root_doc(\n            pk,\n            request,\n            include_deleted=True,\n        )\n        if isinstance(resolved, HttpResponseForbidden):\n            return resolved\n        file_doc = self._get_effective_file_doc(\n            resolved.request_doc,\n            resolved.root_doc,\n            request,\n        )\n        return serve_file(\n            doc=file_doc,\n            use_archive=not self.original_requested(request)\n            and file_doc.has_archive_version,\n            disposition=disposition,\n            follow_formatting=request.query_params.get(\"follow_formatting\", False),\n        )"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "condition": [
            {
              "statement": "The owner-aware check permits an object when it is unowned, owned by the caller, or passes the object permission checker.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/permissions.py",
                  "startLine": 624,
                  "endLine": 635,
                  "quote": "def has_perms_owner_aware(user, perms, obj):\n    \"\"\"\n    Legacy slow path (guardian-backed) single-object permission check.\n\n    The queryset-filtering side of this migrated onto\n    ``PermittedObjectsFilter``/``permitted_object_ids()``, but this\n    single-object check still has many production callers. Several callers\n    remain across ``documents/``, ``paperless_mail/``, and ``paperless_ai/``\n    -- grep for this function name before removing it.\n    \"\"\"\n    checker = ObjectPermissionChecker(user)\n    return obj.owner is None or obj.owner == user or checker.has_perm(perms, obj)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "statement": "When a version is requested, effective-file resolution resolves the requested version for the root rather than using ownership of that version as the root authorization decision.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/views.py",
                  "startLine": 1375,
                  "endLine": 1399,
                  "quote": "    def _resolve_file_doc(self, root_doc: Document, request):\n        version_requested = get_request_version_param(request) is not None\n        resolution = resolve_requested_version_for_root(\n            root_doc,\n            request,\n            include_deleted=version_requested,\n        )\n        if resolution.error == VersionResolutionError.INVALID:\n            raise NotFound(\"Invalid version parameter\")\n        if resolution.document is None:\n            raise Http404\n        return resolution.document\n\n    def _get_effective_file_doc(\n        self,\n        request_doc: Document,\n        root_doc: Document,\n        request: Request,\n    ) -> Document:\n        if (\n            request_doc.root_document_id is not None\n            and get_request_version_param(request) is None\n        ):\n            return request_doc\n        return self._resolve_file_doc(root_doc, request)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "decisiveMissingFacts": [],
        "suggestedObservations": []
      }
    ],
